81:the gray matter images were smoothed with an 6-mm full width at half maximum Gaussian kernel (Ashburner 2009; Han et al. 2021). We also calculated the total intracranial volume (TIV) for the following analysis. The Image Quality Rating (IQR) combing image noise contrast ratio, inhomogeneity contrast ratio and root mean square was recorded to assess images quality (Brown et al. 2019; Han, Xu, Guo, Fang, Wei, et al. 2022a, 2022b, 2022e).
93:its deviates from the normal distribution. Following the previous studies (Marquand et al. 2016; Wolfers et al. 2018), we trained a Gaussian process regression model to predict voxel-wise GMV from age and sex in HCs and then applied the trained model to infer GMV of patients with OCD. For each voxel, the Z -score was obtained by quantifying the deviation between the predicted GMV andthetrueonethennormalizedbytheuncertaintyof prediction. The positive Z -scores suggested increased GMVs than expected in patients than HCs and vice versa. We divided voxel-wise morphological differences into increased and decreased parts according to Z -scores. For decreased parts, the Z -scores were multiplied by -1. The following step was performed in increased and decreased parts separately.
101:Inspired by the previous study (Lee et al. 2022), we proposed a strategy to automatically determine the optimal K from 2 to 6. To be more specific, for each k , we ran NMF 100 times as the algorithm depended on random initialization and the final estimate was obtained by selecting the solution closet to the remaining 99 estimates across runs (Berry et al. 2007). The corresponding factors were matched through the Hungarian matching algorithm (Zhang et al. 2016; Lee et al. 2022). The optimal K was determined when stability value (the averaged pairwise correlation across all latent factors) reached the maximum across runs. The corresponding factors and weights with the optimal K were recorded.
105:To associate the identified disease factors and clinical characteristics, the Pearson's correlation coefficients between factor compositions and clinical characteristics including illness duration, age of onset and symptom severity were calculated. We also investigate whether there were significant differences between female and male patients in terms of factor compositions using two sample t -test.
117:Then, we investigated how the individualized differences contributed to the observed group-level differences. The group-level differences were obtained with two sample t test where age, sex, and TIV were included as covariates. This procedure was done using SPM12 (http://www.fil.ion.ucl.ac.uk/spm). We constructed a linear regression model to predict the group-level differences (unthresholded T map) from the identified 4 disease factors. Here, we supposed that the group-level differences were representative of an 'average' patient and the coefficients of the regression model were assumed as its factor compositions.
